1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,852
No clients yet is not a character flaw. It is a labeling problem. Sample work, personal projects, and clear process still count when you do not pretend they are paid case studies.

2
00:00:12,252 --> 00:00:22,252
The rule. Never claim what did not happen. No fake logos. No invented metrics. No client language for self-assigned practice. Honesty is a feature, not a bug.

3
00:00:22,652 --> 00:00:34,504
Option one. Rebuild something that already exists publicly. Take a real site or product. Redesign one page or rewrite one flow. Show before and after. Label it clearly as a redesign study.

4
00:00:34,904 --> 00:00:47,496
Option two. Solve a real problem for free once. Help a friend, a nonprofit, a local shop, or an open-source project. Document the problem, your process, and the result. Get permission to show it.

5
00:00:47,896 --> 00:00:59,007
Option three. Publish the process itself. A detailed teardown, a how I would fix this series, or a sample deliverable pack. Process transparency builds trust faster than empty case studies.

6
00:00:59,407 --> 00:01:08,667
Labeling. Say exactly what it is. Sample project. Personal study. Pro-bono for this organization. Redesign concept. Never call it client work if it was not.

7
00:01:09,067 --> 00:01:19,437
Evidence. Show the thinking, not just the final pretty picture. Problem statement. Constraints. Decisions you made. What you would do differently next time. That is the real portfolio.

8
00:01:19,837 --> 00:01:33,911
Your next move. Ship one honest piece this week. Pick one of the three options. Produce it. Label it correctly. Put it where people can see it. Then go find the first paid version of the same thing.

